course: dictionary
lesson: 189
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. This dictionary entry for airdrop lists three. In «Several countries dropped food from planes over Gaza when trucks could not bring in enough», airdrop is a noun: the food sent down from the plane is an airdrop.
explain: Airdrop can also be a verb, which is an action. To airdrop something means to drop it from a plane to people on the ground. In «aid groups said airdrops carry far less than trucks», the word airdrops names the supplies sent this way. Look for clues: planes, food, people below.
explain: The third meaning comes from computers. AirDrop, with capital letters, is an Apple feature for sending photos or files to a nearby device, as in «airdrop it to me». Context tells you which meaning is right: planes and aid mean the first meaning, while phones and photos mean the third.
fact: Airdrop (noun) means supplies sent by dropping them from an aircraft, often by parachute.
fact: Airdrop (verb) means to drop supplies from a plane to people on the ground.
fact: In the news, airdrops are often food, water or medicine for people who are cut off from help.
fact: The aid in the example was dropped «when trucks could not bring in enough», so airdrops are used when trucks cannot get through.
fact: AirDrop with capital letters is an Apple feature for sharing files with nearby devices.
exercise: In the news, «aid was airdropped to people cut off», what does airdropped mean? | *Dropped from a plane to people on the ground | Hidden under the sea | Sent by email to a phone | Flown back home quickly
exercise: Ana says, «airdrop it to me». What does airdrop mean here? | Delete the photo from her phone | *Send a file to a nearby device | Crash a plane | Drop something from an aircraft
exercise: In «Several countries dropped food from planes over Gaza», which clue tells you airdrop means supplies from a plane? | The word countries | The word several | The word over | *The words food and planes
test: In «aid groups said airdrops carry far less than trucks», what is an airdrop? | A kind of truck | A soldier's jump | *A load of supplies sent by aircraft | A computer file
test: Which sentence uses airdrop as a verb? | Send the photo by airdrop | The airdrop was heavy and full of food | *Pilots will airdrop food over the village | Her airdrops arrived on Monday
exam: Which clue shows that «airdrop it to me» is about phones and not planes? | *It is a file or photo being sent to someone | It mentions a parachute | The word it | The word airdrop alone
